    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "yaml",
          "# Multi-AZ deployment (Reliability)\nResources:\n  ALB:\n    Type: AWS::ElasticLoadBalancingV2::LoadBalancer\n    Properties:\n      Subnets: [!Ref SubnetA, !Ref SubnetB, !Ref SubnetC]  # 3 AZs\n      \n  AutoScaling:\n    Type: AWS::AutoScaling::AutoScalingGroup\n    Properties:\n      MinSize: 2\n      MaxSize: 10\n      AvailabilityZones: [us-east-1a, us-east-1b, us-east-1c]\n\n# Encryption everywhere (Security)\n  Database:\n    Type: AWS::RDS::DBInstance\n    Properties:\n      StorageEncrypted: true\n      \n  Bucket:\n    Type: AWS::S3::Bucket\n    Properties:\n      BucketEncryption:\n        ServerSideEncryptionConfiguration:\n          - ServerSideEncryptionByDefault:\n              SSEAlgorithm: AES256"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "bash",
          "# Use the Well-Architected Tool in AWS Console\n# Or programmatically:\naws wellarchitected create-workload \\\n  --workload-name \"Production API\" \\\n  --environment PRODUCTION \\\n  --lenses wellarchitected \\\n  --aws-regions us-east-1\n\n# Answer lens questions and get recommendations\naws wellarchitected list-answers \\\n  --workload-id xxx \\\n  --lens-alias wellarchitected \\\n  --pillar-id security"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Ask yourself for each workload:\n\u25a1 Can it survive an AZ failure? (Reliability)\n\u25a1 Is all data encrypted? (Security)\n\u25a1 Are there runbooks for incidents? (Operational Excellence)\n\u25a1 Could we scale 10x without redesign? (Performance)\n\u25a1 Are we paying for idle resources? (Cost)\n\u25a1 Are we using the most efficient instance types? (Sustainability)"
        ]
      ]
    }
